"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct RC#1's sibling-module characterization: the 6 non-flagged modules use THREE distinct patterns (module-top try/except in janitor/repo_snapshot/git_fetch, a sys.platform conditional in alert_store, and function-local imports in recent_creates/hlc), not a uniform 'try/except ImportError -> None'.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["search_files found 10 module files importing fcntl in src/rebar","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/alert_store.py:12-15 uses `if sys.platform != \"win32\": import fcntl / else: fcntl = None` (NOT try/except)","src/rebar/_commands/recent_creates.py:64 imports fcntl inside `_journal_lock` (function-local)","src/rebar/_store/hlc.py:106 imports fcntl inside `_hlc_lock` (function-local)","only janitor:69, repo_snapshot:86, git_fetch:25 use module-top `try/except ImportError`"],"finding":"The plan's premise that '6 sibling modules already try/except ImportError -> None' is inaccurate on inspection: only 3 modules use module-top `try/except ImportError` (janitor:69-72, repo_snapshot:86-89, git_fetch:25-28); alert_store:12-15 uses an `if sys.platform != \"win32\": import fcntl` form; and recent_creates:64 and hlc:106 use FUNCTION-LOCAL imports (inside `_journal_lock`/`_hlc_lock`), not the module-top try/except pattern described.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9db81d95212a03ba","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan (Phase 2) RC#1: '6 sibling modules already try/except ImportError -> None'","norm_id":"n33d0fcc8d24efeb5","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author or checker relies on the '6 modules use try/except' invariant to define what 'guarded' means for the new AST checker"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Acknowledge that _network_guard patches BOTH socket.socket.connect and socket.create_connection, and state how the family-narrowing fix treats each (which seam gains the AF_INET/AF_INET6-only check and whether create_connection is left as-is).","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["tests/conftest.py:324-333 — the guard enters BOTH `patch.object(socket.socket, \"connect\", _guard_socket_connect)` AND `patch(\"socket.create_connection\", side_effect=RuntimeError(...))`","RC#2 describes only 'patches socket.socket.connect for ALL families'"],"finding":"RC#2 states the network guard 'patches socket.socket.connect for ALL families', but tests/conftest.py's _network_guard patches BOTH `socket.socket.connect` AND `socket.create_connection`. The fix plan and AC narrow only the connect path to AF_INET/AF_INET6; the create_connection patch (which raises unconditionally) is not mentioned, leaving its disposition under the family-narrowing fix unspecified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7a404c17c78b7110","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan (Phase 2) RC#2 and AC: 'network guard blocks only AF_INET/AF_INET6; AF_UNIX allowed'","norm_id":"n035915221a4b5c5e","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer narrows only socket.socket.connect and leaves socket.create_connection patched to raise; the AF_INET 'teeth' AC could then pass via create_connection while the described single-seam narrowing is incomplete or the two patches drift"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the sibling-guard inventory (try/except, `sys.platform` conditional, and function-local deferred imports are all legitimate) and specify that the AST guard's true-negative tests accept ALL three shapes — flagging only genuinely unconditional module-top `import fcntl`.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: '6 sibling modules already try/except ImportError -> None'","alert_store.py:12-15 uses `if sys.platform != \"win32\": import fcntl` else `fcntl = None` — NOT try/except","recent_creates.py:64 and hlc.py:106 use function-local `import fcntl` inside a contextmanager — never at module top, so they never break collection","AST guard AC promises 'true-positive + true-negative + refactor-survival tests' but does not enumerate these three distinct true-negative shapes"],"finding":"The plan's characterization of the existing guarded siblings as '6 sibling modules already try/except ImportError -> None' is inaccurate, and the inaccuracy is load-bearing for the structural guard's true-negative coverage. The live code shows THREE distinct legitimate patterns: try/except ImportError (janitor.py, repo_snapshot.py, git_fetch.py), a `sys.platform != 'win32'` conditional (alert_store.py:12-15), and FUNCTION-LOCAL deferred imports (recent_creates.py:64, hlc.py:106) that never break `import rebar`. The AST guard for unguarded module-level `import fcntl` must accept the sys.platform conditional form as guarded AND must not flag function-local imports, otherwise it either false-positives on compliant code or under-defines what 'module-level' means.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc959b76b66efe984","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan RC#1; AC line 'Structural guard scripts/check_fcntl_import_guard.py'","norm_id":"nd3f9f4d588828e53","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The AST guard flags alert_store.py's sys.platform-conditional import as unguarded (false positive), breaking make lint on already-compliant code","The guard's true-negative test only covers the try/except shape, so a future refactor to the sys.platform form silently trips the guard"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"State that the guard accepts an `import fcntl` as guarded when it is under a try/except-ImportError OR a `sys.platform` conditional OR is function-local (not module-top), and add a true-negative test case for each of the three live shapes (git_fetch.py, alert_store.py, hlc.py).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify in the structural-guard AC which guard forms the AST checker accepts as 'guarded' (at minimum: try/except ImportError, a sys.platform-conditional module-level import per alert_store.py, and function-local imports) so it does not false-positive on already-portable modules.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.13,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/alert_store.py:12-15 — `if sys.platform != \"win32\": import fcntl` is a module-LEVEL import not wrapped in try/except","the AC's 'true-negative + refactor-survival tests' language implies the checker must not fire on already-guarded modules"],"finding":"The structural-guard AC says the checker 'fails on any unguarded module-level import fcntl' but does not specify which guard shapes it treats as acceptable. The codebase contains a module-level `import fcntl` guarded by `if sys.platform != \"win32\":` (alert_store.py:12-15) rather than try/except; unless the AST checker recognizes the platform-conditional (and function-local) forms as guarded, it will emit a false positive against alert_store.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff6c2f8ee072d4ec6","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria: 'Structural guard scripts/check_fcntl_import_guard.py ... fails on any unguarded module-level import fcntl in src/rebar'","norm_id":"n421adf2828829962","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["make lint runs the new checker against the full src/rebar tree, which includes alert_store's platform-conditional module-level import"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify (or trim) the three-layer enforcement for the P3 fcntl invariant: confirm the bespoke AST guard AND its true-positive/true-negative/refactor-survival test-trio add value beyond the RED→GREEN `import rebar` pytest regression, or drop the redundant layer.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7667,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan AC: 'Structural guard scripts/check_fcntl_import_guard.py (AST; stdlib-only, wired into make lint) ... ships true-positive + true-negative + refactor-survival tests'","Plan AC also already ships: 'RED→GREEN: the 4 modules import under simulated non-POSIX (sys.modules['fcntl']=None) and import rebar succeeds — proven by pytest tests/unit/test_fcntl_import_guard.py' — this alone catches the regression class","Severity: P3, 'Mirror/experimental tier — non-blocking. CI-hygiene / cross-platform-portability signal.'","Codebase: ~45 check_*.py structural guards already exist in scripts/ wired into make lint (established pattern), so the AST-guard PATTERN itself is not NIH — the concern is the three-layer redundancy for one P3 invariant, not the tool choice"],"finding":"For a P3 non-blocking mirror-tier hygiene fix, the plan ships three overlapping enforcement mechanisms for one invariant (no unguarded module-level `import fcntl`): a RED→GREEN pytest regression (test_fcntl_import_guard.py), a NEW stdlib AST script (check_fcntl_import_guard.py) wired into `make lint`, AND that script's OWN dedicated three-case test suite (true-positive + true-negative + refactor-survival). The pytest regression already proves the runtime invariant (`import rebar` succeeds under `sys.modules['fcntl']=None`); the incremental value of a bespoke AST guard PLUS a three-case meta-test suite is future-reintroduction prevention, which is real but is heavier than the severity warrants. Confirm this is justified rather than trimming the AST script's dedicated test-trio (or the AST script itself) to keep the fix proportionate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f122dce00a349ea3b","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — the `scripts/check_fcntl_import_guard.py` AC line and the `test_fcntl_import_guard.py` AC line","norm_id":"nc5c4d95316df88c3","priority":0.1833,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer/maintainer maintaining three parallel artifacts (pytest regression, AST script, AST-script meta-tests) that all enforce the same single invariant on a non-gating tier"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low",